\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2011\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WORSE-THAN-EXPECTED BOJ TANKAN SHOWS IMPACT OF HIGH YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business sentiment among large Japanese manufacturers worsened more than expected in the three months to December, the BOJ's closely watched tankan survey showed Thursday, as the yen's strength, the deepening euro-zone debt crisis and flooding in Thailand darkened the economic outlook. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULD NOT OVERREACT TO RECENT DECLINE IN YUAN AGAINST DOLLAR - ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should not overreact to the yuan's recent decline against the U.S. dollar as unnecessary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities will hinder exchange rate reforms and internationalization of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as well as risks the country being labelled a "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator", an economist with a government think tank wrote in a commentary on the state-run China Daily published Thursday. (published 0123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HIGHLIGHTS LIMITS OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets has only short-lived results that are of limited value, according to a report from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  released Thursday. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXEC SAYS AUSTRALIAN COMPANIES INCREASING A$ BETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian companies are queuing up to hedge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk amid growing concern of a sharp correction in the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , an executive at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN INFLATION EXPECTATIONS NUDGE LOWER IN DECEMBER -SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian inflationary expectations nudged lower in December from November reflecting growing pessimism among consumers as unemployment rises and the outlook for the world economy looks increasingly grim. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN RBA SOLD A$330M IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold A$330 million in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in November, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH UPGRADES AUSTRALIA'S NEW SOUTH WALES STATE TO AAA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's New South Wales state, home of the country's largest city Sydney, was upgraded to AAA from AA+ by Fitch Ratings on Wednesday. (published 2243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND'S MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY FURTHER CONTRACTS IN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing activity further contracted in November and is at its lowest level since June 2009, data released Thursday show. (published 2203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES JOBLESS RATE EASES TO 6.4% IN OCTOBER VS 7.1% IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The unemployment rate in the Philippines eased to 6.4% in October from 7.1% in July, data from the National Statistics Office showed Thursday. (published 0155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WSJ: US TREASURY BUYERS FLIP THE SCRIPT DESPITE DATA THAT WOULD HINT AT INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's not the economy, stupid. (published 2322 GMT) [ 15-12-11 0200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111215e7cf0002q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
