\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S 3Q GDP GROWTH POWERED BY MINE INVESTMENT SURGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's A$1.3 trillion commodity-based economy roared in the third quarter as the full force of a huge mining investment boom began to exert itself, though the road ahead is less certain as Europe's future remains far from clear and Asian growth is slowing. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE OFFICIAL: YUAN'S WEAKNESS SHOWS CHINA NOT MANIPULATING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent weakness in the yuan is a good thing, as it shows China is not manipulating its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Chong Quan, the country's deputy trade representative said Wednesday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN FOREIGN RESERVES HIT RECORD HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's foreign reserves hit a record high in November, the Finance Ministry said Wednesday, after aggressive efforts by the government to weaken the yen through market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boosted the country's dollar holdings. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SWAN: BIG BANKS AWASH WITH DOMESTIC DEPOSITS, FUNDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan continued Wednesday to pressure the big four domestic banks to fully pass on to customers a 25-basis-point cut in the official cash rate to 4.25%, announced Tuesday by the Reserve Bank. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA UNVEILS LATEST PLAN TO BOOST PROPERTY MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government Wednesday unveiled its latest plan to boost the ailing property market, seeking to increase the number of transactions and boost the housing supply for renters. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE OFFICIAL: CHINA FACES TOUGH CHALLENGES IN GLOBAL TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will face tough challenges in global trade next year, Wang Shouwen, director of the Foreign Trade Department of the Ministry of Commerce, said Wednesday. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: EXPORT GROWTH MAY SLOW TO 15% IN 2012 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's export growth may slow to 15% in 2012 from an estimated 18% this year amid a weak global recovery and the potentially large drag from the European debt crisis, a government think tank researcher was quoted as saying Wednesday. (published 2353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS PRESSING BANKS TO PASS ON RBA CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan said Wednesday he will continue to pressure the country's biggest banks to pass on in full a 25 basis point rate cut by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as he highlighted the profit margins enjoyed by local lenders as justification to lower borrowing charges. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN LEADING EMPLOYMENT INDICATOR ROSE TO 0.071 IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Department of Education, Employment and Workplace Relations reported Wednesday that its leading indicator of employment rose to 0.071 in December from November. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN PERFORMANCE OF CONSTRUCTION INDEX UP 4.9 POINTS TO 39.6 IN NOV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction activity in Australia improved in November, though remained in contraction for the 18th straight month as Australia's housing market was particularly weak in the past month. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BANKS' MORTGAGE LOAN GROWTH SLOWS IN NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korean banks' household mortgage loans slowed in November on decreased borrowing related to apartment down payments, the Bank of Korea said Wednesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GREEK PARLIAMENT APPROVES 2012 BUDGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's parliament approved early Wednesday the country's 2012 budget, aimed at bringing Greece back on track with deficit targets it has promised international creditors. (published 2350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF CHIEF: FUND PREPARED TO PROVIDE FINANCING IN MIDDLE EAST, NORTH AFRICA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund is ready to help finance economic reform in the Middle East and North Africa, Managing Director Christine Lagarde said Tuesday. (published 2216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HANA BANK SEEKS TO PRICE DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD AROUND TSYS +370 BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Hana Bank, the flagship unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hana Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., is seeking to price a benchmark 5.5-year dollar bond to yield around 370 basis points over comparable Treasury yields as early as Wednesday, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WSJ: ECB CURBS BAR SOME BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prepares to meet for the first time since last week's move to ease the funding strains on Europe's troubled banks, Wall Street is speculating about whether it may do even more. (published 0219 GMT) [ 07-12-11 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par