\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie & kiwi retreat vs USD, await RBA decision\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2011\par 22:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON/SYDNEY, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars were lower on a broadly stronger U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday in the wake of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen, while investors bet \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut rates for the first time in over two years.\par \par \uc2 * Aussie trading around $1.0540 , having ranged between $1.0507 and $1.0611 overnight, but little changed from Monday's late local level.\par \par \uc2 * It slid 1.5 pct on Monday after Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell massive amounts of yen for U.S. dollars, lifting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board.\par \par \uc2 * Yet the Aussie still gained 9 percent in October, its second biggest monthly increase on record. Near term support seen at Monday's daily low at $1.0505 and resistance at $1.0640.\par \par \uc2 * The New Zealand dollar trades around $0.8070, just below Monday's late local level, after ranging $0.8080 to $0.8144 overnight.\par \par \uc2 * Kiwi gained 6.2 percent in October, best since May 2009. Near term support kicks in at $0.8050 below that $0.8010, with $0.8160 to cap the upside.\par \par \uc2 * Market awaiting outcome of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's (RBA) policy meeting at 0030 GMT which could well deliver the first cut in rates since April 2009.\par \par \uc2 * Interbank market implies around an 84 percent chance of a 25 bps easing to 4.5 pct <0#YIB:>. A Reuters poll found 12 of 19 analysts looked for a cut .\par \par \uc2 * Recent data showing inflation much less of a threat than initially feared gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to take policy towards a more neutral setting. Aussie could rebound if the RBA stays on hold.\par \par \uc2 * The Aussie halves its gains on the yen to 82.29 yen\par \par \uc2 , after rising as high of 83.90 when Japan entered the market to buy U.S. dollars for yen. Kiwi also retreats to 63.05 yen , from a peak of 64.54 yen.\par \par \uc2 * Against the kiwi, the Aussie firmer at NZ$1.3044, from NZ$1.2994. Last week the Aussie hit a 4-1/2 month high of NZ$1.3125.\par \par \uc2 * New Zealand has third-quarter labour market data later on Tuesday, with expectations of a modest lift in wages and jobs. Unemployment numbers on Thursday with the jobless rate forecast at 6.4 percent, from 6.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 * New Zealand government bond prices <0#NZTSY=> firmer, with yields down 4 basis points along the curve. U.S. Treasuries soar amid weak stocks and bankruptcy of futures brokerage.\par \par \uc2 * Australian debt futures gained, with the three-year contract <YTTc1> 0.09 points higher at 96.190 and the 10-year <YTCc1> up 0.10 points at 95.560.\par \par \uc2 * The euro tumbles more than 2 percent against the dollar as investors' expectations cool over last week's European measures to stem the debt crisis, raising risk aversion. The dollar also fares well against the Swiss franc .\par \par \uc2 (Australia/New Zealand bureaux)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111103e7av001kz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
