\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ RBA Battellino: Uptrend In Global Inflation Makes Policy Calls Harder\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2011\par 06:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:24 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: China Now A Source Of World Inflation\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:25 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: Australian Fiscal Situation Very Solid\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:27 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: Global Market Conditions Different From 2008\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:31 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: Current Circumstances Don't Warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:31 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: Australian Dollar Level Consistent With Terms Of Trade\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 00:35 EDT *DJ  RBA Battellino: US Fed Reaching Limits Of What Policy Can Do\par \par \uc2 23 Aug 2011 01:09 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Circumstances Don't Warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The current elevated levels of the Australian dollar don't warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Ric Battellino\uc2 , Deputy Governor of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 , said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Moving to damp the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength "would have no meaningful effect," Battellino told a conference.\par \par \uc2 The surge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over recent years is in line with gains in prices for the commodities Australia exports. "What happened with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mirrors what happened with the terms of trade," Battellino said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched 30-year highs in August above US$1.1080, levels that have hurt the country's exporters of manufactured goods. At 0450 GMT, the Australian dollar was trading at US$1.0451.\par \par \uc2 Lost export competitiveness was blamed for the announcement this week by \uc2 BlueScope Steel Ltd\uc2 . (BSL.AU) that it will shut down some \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and lay off 1,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Still, Battellino said conditions globally weren't yet as bad as those seen in 2008 after the collapse of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "(Australia's) banks have had no trouble obtaining funds. It is a very different situation to 2008," he said.\par \par \uc2 The last time the RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was to support the Australian dollar as it lost 40% in value in late 2008.\par \par \uc2 -By James Glynn, Dow Jones Newswires; 61-2-8272-4685; james.glynn@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 23, 2011 01:09 ET (05:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110823e78n000u9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
