\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 23\b0\par\par\uc2 1,802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2011\par 09:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MINISTRY: FOREIGN TRADE FACES SLOW EXTERNAL DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's foreign trade is facing slow external demand and pressure from surging costs, while the debt crisis in developed countries also poses greater challenges for emerging economies including China, the Ministry of Commerce said Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  FLASH PMI SHOWS CHINA MANUFACTURING SLOWING, HARD LANDING RISK LIMITED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The preliminary HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index reading for August increased slightly but showed that manufacturing activity contracted for a second straight month. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SHORT-TERM DEBT GROWTH SLOWS SHARPLY ON GOVERNMENT STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's short-term external debt slowed significantly in the second quarter, while new long-term borrowing accelerated, indicating the government's efforts to shift offshore borrowing to a more stable profile and reduce the risk of sudden rapid capital outflows are having an effect. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: WATCHING EFFECTS OF YEN ON ECON, WILL ACT PROPERLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa reiterated Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is paying close attention to the negative effects of recent yen rises and stands ready to take further measures to counter the impact of the strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the nation's export-dependant economy. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: CHECKING IF THERE ARE ANY SPECULATIVE MOVES IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister said Tuesday that the government is checking to see if there have been any speculative moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as the yen has stayed firm, reflecting concerns about the U.S. and European economies. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN KAIEDA: IMPORTANT TO TAKE RESOLUTE ACTION IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's trade minister Tuesday called for the government not to let its guard down against speculators affecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM'S RESIGNATION NEARS AS ENERGY BILL CLEARS LOWER HOUSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The end of Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan's term in office moved a step closer Tuesday, as a bill to promote renewable energy cleared the country's lower house of parliament and is set to be voted on by the upper house Friday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : CIRCUMSTANCES DON'T WARRANT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The current elevated levels of the Australian dollar don't warrant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ric Battellino\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Deputy Governor of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Tuesday. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SAYS GLOBAL JITTERS BIG POLICY CHALLENGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to grapple with the extreme uncertainty in the global financial markets, saying it could be months before the fallout settles. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S TREASURER WANTS ALL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO FLOAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan said Tuesday all countries should allow the free float of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and rejected a call to establish a sovereign wealth fund to store some of the returns from the commodities boom to moderate the impact on the economy of the strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE INFLATION ACCELERATES; MAS FACES TOUGH BALANCING ACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer inflation rate unexpectedly accelerated in July, driven by stubbornly high prices for food, housing and cars and underscoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's concern that inflationary pressure persists even as growth slows. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ANZ BANKING TO RAISE A$750M FROM HYBRID CAPITAL ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to raise 750 million Australian dollars to give it the flexibility for timing when it redeems subordinated debt and other capital instruments. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN'S CHINA STEEL SEEKS UP TO NT$20 BLN VIA BONDS; PLANS INDIA EXPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Taiwan's largest steel producer by revenue, said Tuesday it plans to raise up to NT$20 billion via bonds that will carry maturities of three to seven years. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA TELECOM 1H NET PROFIT UP 8% ON 3G MOBILE SERVICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Network operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Telecom Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday reported slightly better-than-expected first-half net profit growth as subscriber numbers for its mobile services grew in the face of intensifying competition. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AXIATA GROUP 2Q NET PROFIT UP 15%; EXPECTS CHALLENGES AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Axiata Group Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its second-quarter net profit rose 15% on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, but Malaysia's biggest mobile operator by revenue said it expects to face challenges in the remaining months of this year due to a strengthening Malaysia ringgit and softness in its major markets. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA REGULATOR APPROVES XCMG CONSTRUCTION TO SELL UP TO 593M SHARES IN HK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's securities regulator has approved \f28 \uc2 \f2 XCMG Construction Machinery Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s plan to sell up to 593 million shares in a Hong Kong initial public offering, the Shenzhen-listed company said in a statement Tuesday. (published 2355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF AMERICA\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO KEEP \f28 \uc2 \f2 CHINA CONSTRUCTION BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese banking officials said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will keep at least half of its 10% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Construction Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., disappointing investors who hoped the largest U.S. bank by assets would sell more of the Chinese lender's shares. (published 2229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MICROSOFT INKS CLOUD-COMPUTING PACT WITH CHINA SOFTWARE COMPANY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Microsoft Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it signed a pact with Linux operating-system provider China Standard Software Co. to jointly develop, market and sell products and services in China's cloud-computing market. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SGX CEO: SINGAPORE LISTING OFFERS COMPANIES BROADER REGIONAL REACH THAN HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magnus Bocker\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday said the city-state was an able competitor to Hong Kong in the race to attract companies from outside Asia to list. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MIRVAC LAST FY NET PROFIT FALLS 22% TO A$182.3 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Office and residential property investor and developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mirvac Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its net profit fell 22% to A$182.3 million in the last fiscal year ended June 30 from A$234.7 million a year earlier, reflecting the impact of previously announced provisions for losses on inventories for projects in regional areas. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL SEARCH 1H PROFIT MORE THAN DOUBLES; SAYS PNG LNG ON TRACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil Search Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday said first half profit more than doubled due to higher oil prices and it moved to address concerns that regime change in Papau New Guinea will affect its US$15 billion gas export joint venture with \f28 \uc2 \f2 ExxonMobil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ANZ BANKING TO RAISE A$750M FROM HYBRID CAPITAL ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to raise 750 million Australian dollars to give it the flexibility for timing when it redeems subordinated debt and other capital instruments. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CONSOLIDATED EXPECTS FOXTEL BID FOR AUSTAR TO PROCEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian media investment company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Consolidated Media Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., part owner of Australia's largest pay television operator Foxtel, said Tuesday it expects Foxtel's 1.9 billion Australian dollar bid for fellow pay television company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Austar United Communications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to go ahead after regulators initially questioned the deal. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GAS NEGARA TO SPEND UP TO IDR1.5 TLN FOR ACQUISITIONS -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian gas distributor \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Perusahaan Gas Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans this year to spend up to IDR1.5 trillion to acquire stakes in several gas and oil blocks in efforts to fulfil the domestic gas demand, an official at the company said. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CONNECTEAST ASSESSOR VALUES COMPANY AT 51-57C/SECURITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ConnectEast Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that an independent expert has valued the company's securities at 51 cents to 57 cents each and concluded that a takeover offer from Horizon Roads at 55 cents is fair and reasonable. (published 2245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: FOSTER'S FENDS OFF \f28 \uc2 \f2 SABMILLER\f28 \uc2 \f2  WITH A$500M SHAREHOLDER RETURN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foster's Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it would return at least 500 million Australian dollars to shareholders as the board attempts to ward off a hostile takeover bid from SABMiller Group PLC . (published 0402 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ 2nd UPDATE: FORD, TOYOTA TEAM UP ON GAS-ELECTRIC HYBRID SYSTEM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An unusual pairing of major auto makers is seeking to develop a gas-electric hybrid system for light trucks and sport-utility vehicles, a move to share the cost of new technology as both work to achieve the latest U.S. fuel-economy targets set by the Obama administration. (published 2344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ORIGIN FY PROFIT IN LINE; TIPS 30% GROWTH THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Origin Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Australia's biggest electricity retailer, on Tuesday booked a steep decline in full-year profit largely owing to costs associated with the acquisition of power assets in New South Wales state. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; CHINA \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  PMI INJECTS SOME OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mostly higher as China's manufacturing activity eased concerns of a downturn in the world's second largest economy, injecting some confidence to recently battered markets. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SHANGHAI GOLD EXCHANGE RAISES TRADING MARGIN TO 12%; CURB DEFAULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Gold Exchange said Tuesday that it will raise the margin for gold trading to 12% from the current 11% starting at the Aug. 25 market settlement, and will increase the intraday limit for price movements in gold to 9% from 7% starting Aug. 26. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BHP SEEKS TO RECRUIT BLUESCOPE'S LAID-OFF WORKERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 23-08-11 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will seek to plug a number of job vacancies at its coal and iron ore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Australia, recruiting workers set to be laid off by struggling steel producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 BlueScope Steel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN YET TO COVER 60% OF OCTOBER-DECEMBER FEED CORN IMPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan has yet to purchase around 60% of its feed corn import requirements for the October-December period, and buyers are awaiting a downward correction in prices, trading executives said Tuesday. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GAS NEGARA TO SPEND UP TO IDR1.5 TLN FOR ACQUISITIONS -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian gas distributor \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Perusahaan Gas Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans this year to spend up to IDR1.5 trillion to acquire stakes in several gas and oil blocks in efforts to fulfil the domestic gas demand, an official at the company said. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA PETRONAS: TO START MYR15 BLN UPSTREAM PROJECT WITH PARTNERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian state oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroliam Nasional Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Petronas, said Tuesday that it is embarking on a MYR15 billion upstream project with partners, tapping gas reserves in marginal fields offshore Malaysia to meet the country's growing demand. (published 0343 GMT) [ 23-08-11 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110823e78n000hr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
