\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2011\par 08:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MINISTRY: FOREIGN TRADE FACES SLOW EXTERNAL DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's foreign trade is facing slow external demand and pressure from surging costs, while the debt crisis in developed countries also poses greater challenges for emerging economies including China, the Ministry of Commerce said Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  FLASH PMI SHOWS CHINA MANUFACTURING SLOWING, HARD LANDING RISK LIMITED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The preliminary HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index reading for August increased slightly but showed that manufacturing activity contracted for a second straight month. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA SHORT-TERM DEBT GROWTH SLOWS SHARPLY ON GOVERNMENT STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's short-term external debt slowed significantly in the second quarter, while new long-term borrowing accelerated, indicating the government's efforts to shift offshore borrowing to a more stable profile and reduce the risk of sudden rapid capital outflows are having an effect. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: CHECKING IF THERE ARE ANY SPECULATIVE MOVES IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister said Tuesday that the government is checking to see if there have been any speculative moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as the yen has stayed firm, reflecting concerns about the U.S. and European economies. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN KAIEDA: IMPORTANT TO TAKE RESOLUTE ACTION IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's trade minister Tuesday called for the government not to let its guard down against speculators affecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN PM'S RESIGNATION NEARS AS ENERGY BILL CLEARS LOWER HOUSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The end of Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan's term in office moved a step closer Tuesday, as a bill to promote renewable energy cleared the country's lower house of parliament and is set to be voted on by the upper house Friday. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : CIRCUMSTANCES DON'T WARRANT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The current elevated levels of the Australian dollar don't warrant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ric Battellino\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Deputy Governor of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Tuesday. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SAYS GLOBAL JITTERS BIG POLICY CHALLENGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to grapple with the extreme uncertainty in the global financial markets, saying it could be months before the fallout settles. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SWISS JULY EXPORTS RISE 4.8% ON YEAR IN REAL TERMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss exports increased in July, fueled by demand in Asia for the country's watches, although sales to the European Union were hit by the appreciation of the Swiss franc. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBNZ 3Q SURVEY: FIRMS SEE 1-YEAR AHEAD CPI +2.94% VS +3.12% IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business managers in New Zealand expect inflation pressures to ease over this year and next, the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's third-quarter survey released Tuesday showed. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE JULY CPI +5.4% ON YEAR; DJ POLL TIPPED +5.0% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer price index rose 5.4% on year in July, faster than analysts expected, driven by high housing, food and car prices, and underscoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's view that inflationary pressures remain in the economy. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAKSIN CALLS FOR THAI RECONCILIATION, DOESN'T SPECIFY WHEN TO RETURN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ousted Thai leader Thaksin Shinawatra Tuesday called for reconciliation within Thailand and said he will return to the nation when conditions are right. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIR LIQUIDE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL OFFSHORE YUAN-DENOMINATED BONDS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air Liquide S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue offshore yuan-denominated bonds and will meet investors in Hong Kong from Thursday, people familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ANZ BANKING TO RAISE A$750M FROM HYBRID CAPITAL ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it plans to raise 750 million Australian dollars to give it the flexibility for timing when it redeems subordinated debt and other capital instruments. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 23-08-11 0606GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2