\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,098 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2011\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN FIN MIN: CAN'T SOLVE DEBT CRISIS WITH A SINGLE SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's debt crisis isn't over and discipline needs to be maintained to stop it spreading further, according to German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble. (published 0918 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S CUTS CYPRUS RATING 2 NOTCHES ON FISCAL, POLITICAL, GREECE CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Wednesday downgraded Cyprus by two notches and warned it may cut its rating further, citing its weak fiscal position, fractious political climate, and exposure of the country's banks to Greece. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPAIN, ITALY BONDS FALL, BUNDS RISE ON SCHAEUBLE REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish and Italian bonds fell and safe-haven German bunds rose Wednesday after Reuters reported that German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble had said Berlin opposes a carte blanche for the euro zone's bailout fund to buy government bonds in the secondary market. (published 0848 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SWAN SAYS WON'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO ADJUST AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Treasurer Wayne Swan ruled out the possibility of direct government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease pressure on the resource-rich nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after it surged Wednesday to a record high against the U.S. dollar since it floated in 1983. (published 0907 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY POSTS SHARP JULY DROP IN BUSINESS CONFIDENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's business confidence fell notably more than expected in July, hitting its lowest point since June 2010, led by dimming hopes for orders, national statistics agency Istat said Wednesday. (published 0912 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OSLO CENTRAL STATION RE-OPENS AFTER BOMB SCARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norway police have re-opened Oslo central train station after no suspicious items were found in the luggage searched on a bus there earlier in the morning. (published 1004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH FIN MIN URGES OPPOSITION TO VOTE FOR BALANCED BUDGET RULE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Francois Baroin Wednesday urged opposition Socialists to vote for an amendment to the French constitution requiring a balanced budget. (published 0818 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RUSSIA FACES CRISIS IF PUTIN RETURNS: KREMLIN ADVISERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW --Russia faces a massive crisis including economic collapse and social tensions if Vladimir Putin rather than Dmitry Medvedev stands in presidential polls, two Kremlin advisers warned Wednesday. (published 1012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA 2Q GDP SLOWS; GROWTH TO ACCELERATE IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic growth slowed in the second quarter after rising at the fastest clip in three quarters in the January-March period, as exports weighed amid growing external uncertainties over the euro-zone credit crisis and a potential U.S. debt default. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR HITS FRESH 30-YEAR HIGH AFTER CPI DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar reached a fresh 30-year high Wednesday as surging inflation in the second quarter raised the prospect of a near-term rate hike by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER REMAINS VIGILANT ON STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister reiterated Wednesday that he will remain vigilant against the strengthening yen, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  marked a fresh four-month high against the dollar Tuesday. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA UNLIKELY TO HIKE RESERVE RATIO IN JULY, AUGUST - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is unlikely to hike banks' reserve requirement ratio this month or in August, partly because speculative fund flows have fallen, a reporter for the state-run China Securities Journal wrote in an opinion piece published Wednesday. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE COMMERCE MIN: US DEBT ISSUE HAS YET TO REACH A CONCLUSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Vice Minister of Commerce Wang Chao Wednesday said the U.S. debt ceiling issue is a matter of concern. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULD ADJUST MONETARY POLICY TO AID SMALL, MEDIUM COMPANIES -PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should adjust monetary policy to aid small and medium companies, while still maintaining an overall tight policy setting, a local newspaper backed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a commentary piece Wednesday. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: US DESERVES RATINGS CUT, EX-CHINA WEALTH FUND STRATEGIST SAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. deserves a ratings downgrade and a default can't be ruled out, a former strategist for China's sovereign wealth fund said. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ KAMEZAKI CONCERNED COS MAY SHIFT MORE OUTPUT OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board member Hidetoshi Kamezaki said Wednesday he is greatly concerned that Japanese companies could increasingly shift production overseas due to factors such as a higher yen and worries about the electricity supply. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : ELEVATED INFLATIONARY PRESSURES PROMPTED RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai inflationary pressure remains at an elevated level, prompting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its policy interest rate 25 basis points at its July 13 policy meeting to maintain economic stability and anchor inflation expectations, minutes of the meeting released Wednesday showed. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P'S SHARMA: GOVERNMENTS SHOULDN'T MEDDLE IN RATINGS' PROCESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sovereign governments shouldn't pressure ratings firms to inflate their debt ratings, Standard and Poor's President Deven Sharma said in prepared remarks to be delivered at a hearing Wednesday. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: NO RESPITE FOR WEAK USD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Further EUR gains to 1.4556 are expected, bringing the July 4 reaction high at 1.4580 and the 1.618 Fibonacci extension target at 1.4592 within striking distance. Tuesday's gains completed a bullish continuation pattern on the 60-minute chart, which has created room for a wave equality target at 1.4626. Corrective weakness will attract support while above 1.4422, and only below there would question the positive EUR outlook. (published 0704 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: KEY RESISTANCE UNDER THREAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Tuesday's strength creates room for more bull pressure on key resistance at 128.61. A fresh wave of bull pressure is required to force a break through 128.61, paving the way for more gains to the 129.25 area. Failure to force a break above 128.61, combined with a push to 128.17, would turn the tone bearish, prompting weakness to Tuesday's low at 127.76. (published 0706 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : ASIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SCALE NEW HEIGHTS ON U.S. DEBT WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soared to new highs against the dollar Wednesday, as investors showed the greenback no mercy on increasing expectations the U.S. will lose its triple-A credit rating. (published 0323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: S KOREA JULY CPI LIKELY +4.4%; FACTORY OUTPUT, EXPORTS GROWTH LIKELY FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's consumer inflation likely remained high in July, driven by increases in food prices stemming from the tough monsoon season and demand-side price pressures. (published 0130 GMT) [ 27-07-11 0930GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020110727e77r00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
