\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2011\par 13:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF OFFICIAL LENDING IN NEW GREEK AID LIKELY LESS THAN A THIRD-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund, concerned about its enormous long-term exposure to the euro zone, is likely to contribute less than one-third of official financing in the new Greek aid package, according to people familiar with the situation. (published 1036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NOURIEL ROUBINI SAYS IRELAND, PORTUGAL ARE INSOLVENT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new rescue package for Greece agreed by European leaders last week would at best buy time, the head of Roubini Global Economics is quoted as saying. Euro-zone politicians "may muddle through for another five years", but ultimately they will face "very touch decisions". (published 1037 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK MANUFACTURERS OUTPUT EXPECTATIONS FALL - CBI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. manufacturers' output expectations and order books weakened substantially in July, and their pricing power also appeared to drop off sharply, suggesting the economy got off to a slow start in the third quarter. (published 1100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN FIN MIN: CAN'T SOLVE DEBT CRISIS WITH A SINGLE SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's debt crisis isn't over and discipline needs to be maintained to stop it spreading further, according to German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schaeuble. (published 0918 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMAN FIN MIN ADMITS TO ANGER OVER EURO CRISIS- REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a glimpse of the stress weighing on European policy makers, the German finance minister says he realizes the importance of saving the euro zone but can't help feeling angry sometimes. (published 1039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S CUTS CYPRUS RATING 2 NOTCHES ON FISCAL, POLITICAL, GREECE CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Wednesday downgraded Cyprus by two notches and warned it may cut its rating further, citing its weak fiscal position, fractious political climate, and exposure of the country's banks to Greece. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPAIN, ITALY BONDS FALL ON SCHAEUBLE LETTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moves to allow the European Financial Stability Facility, or EFSF, to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in secondary bond markets and stop funding costs for vulnerable euro-zone countries rising too high were a key element of last week's emergency package to support Greece and stop its debt crisis spreading throughout the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area. (published 1108 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SWAN SAYS WON'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO ADJUST AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Treasurer Wayne Swan ruled out the possibility of direct government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease pressure on the resource-rich nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after it surged Wednesday to a record high against the U.S. dollar since it floated in 1983. (published 0907 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY POSTS SHARP JULY DROP IN BUSINESS CONFIDENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's business confidence fell notably more than expected in July, hitting its lowest point since June 2010, led by dimming hopes for orders, national statistics agency Istat said Wednesday. (published 0912 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OSLO CENTRAL STATION RE-OPENS AFTER BOMB SCARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norway police have re-opened Oslo central train station after no suspicious items were found in the luggage searched on a bus there earlier in the morning. (published 1004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK TO EXPEL ALL REMAINING LIBYAN EMBASSY STAFF - BBC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. is to expel all remaining Libyan embassy staff based in the country, BBC News reports Wednesday, citing officials at the Foreign Office. (published 1030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH FIN MIN URGES OPPOSITION TO VOTE FOR BALANCED BUDGET RULE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Francois Baroin Wednesday urged opposition Socialists to vote for an amendment to the French constitution requiring a balanced budget. (published 0818 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RUSSIA FACES CRISIS IF PUTIN RETURNS: KREMLIN ADVISERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW --Russia faces a massive crisis including economic collapse and social tensions if Vladimir Putin rather than Dmitry Medvedev stands in presidential polls, two Kremlin advisers warned Wednesday. (published 1012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA 2Q GDP SLOWS; GROWTH TO ACCELERATE IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic growth slowed in the second quarter after rising at the fastest clip in three quarters in the January-March period, as exports weighed amid growing external uncertainties over the euro-zone credit crisis and a potential U.S. debt default. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR HITS FRESH 30-YEAR HIGH AFTER CPI DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar reached a fresh 30-year high Wednesday as surging inflation in the second quarter raised the prospect of a near-term rate hike by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER REMAINS VIGILANT ON STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister reiterated Wednesday that he will remain vigilant against the strengthening yen, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  marked a fresh four-month high against the dollar Tuesday. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA UNLIKELY TO HIKE RESERVE RATIO IN JULY, AUGUST - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is unlikely to hike banks' reserve requirement ratio this month or in August, partly because speculative fund flows have fallen, a reporter for the state-run China Securities Journal wrote in an opinion piece published Wednesday. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE COMMERCE MIN: US DEBT ISSUE HAS YET TO REACH A CONCLUSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Vice Minister of Commerce Wang Chao Wednesday said the U.S. debt ceiling issue is a matter of concern. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULD ADJUST MONETARY POLICY TO AID SMALL, MEDIUM COMPANIES -PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should adjust monetary policy to aid small and medium companies, while still maintaining an overall tight policy setting, a local newspaper backed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a commentary piece Wednesday. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FORMER PBOC ADVISER: US BANKS' RATINGS SHOULD BE CUT ON WEAK FUNDAMENTALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former adviser to the People's Bank of China Wednesday said that ratings on U.S. banks should be downgraded as their fundamentals are weak. (published 1139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par BOJ KAMEZAKI CONCERNED COS MAY SHIFT MORE OUTPUT OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan policy board member Hidetoshi Kamezaki said Wednesday he is greatly concerned that Japanese companies could increasingly shift production overseas due to factors such as a higher yen and worries about the electricity supply. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: NO RESPITE FOR WEAK USD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Further EUR gains to 1.4556 are expected, bringing the July 4 reaction high at 1.4580 and the 1.618 Fibonacci extension target at 1.4592 within striking distance. Tuesday's gains completed a bullish continuation pattern on the 60-minute chart, which has created room for a wave equality target at 1.4626. Corrective weakness will attract support while above 1.4422, and only below there would question the positive EUR outlook. (published 0704 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: KEY RESISTANCE UNDER THREAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Tuesday's strength creates room for more bull pressure on key resistance at 128.61. A fresh wave of bull pressure is required to force a break through 128.61, paving the way for more gains to the 129.25 area. Failure to force a break above 128.61, combined with a push to 128.17, would turn the tone bearish, prompting weakness to Tuesday's low at 127.76. (published 0706 GMT) [ 27-07-11 1103GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020110727e77r00018\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
