\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Stronger, Moving Beyond China Rate Hike, German Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephen L. Bernard   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2011\par 23:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The euro climbed against the dollar Tuesday after traders moved beyond a second straight disappointing report on Germany's economy and an interest-rate hike by China.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also quickly fended off a modest advance by the dollar after Richmond Federal Reserve President Jeffrey Lacker said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reconsider its bond purchase program as the U.S. economy gets stronger.\par \par \uc2 Some risk appetite returned to the market as traders downplayed the larger-than-expected drop in Germany industrial production in December. Monday's disappointing report on manufacturing likely tempered expectations heading into the industrial production report and bad weather likely contributed to the poor figures, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would raise benchmark lending and deposit rates by 0.25 percentage point. The move is aimed at further blunting rapid growth and inflation.\par \par \uc2 Traders also bought the euro on news that banks showed low demand for European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  emergency funding on Tuesday, a move that pushed up short-term interest rates in Europe's money markets. Higher rates can make the euro more attractive to investors.\par \par \uc2 "The big thing for the euro today was the low uptake in the ECB's repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Daniel Katzive, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York. The euro's climb lost momentum on Tuesday only when a jump in U.S. Treasury yields started making the dollar more attractive to yield-hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 Eurogroup President Jean-Claude Juncker also tried to assuage investors worried about ongoing sovereign debt issues. Juncker said he expects euro zone leaders to hammer out a comprehensive plan to deal with the debt problems by the end of March. Leaders appeared to make little headway toward a new program during a meeting late last week.\par \par \uc2 Late on Tuesday, the euro was at $1.3625 from about $1.3582 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y82.37 from Y82.32, while the euro was at Y112.25 from Y111.82. The U.K. pound was at $1.6074 from $1.6108. The dollar was at CHF0.9632 from CHF0.9555.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 77.991 from about 78.029.\par \par \uc2 The dollar couldn't sustain the modest bounce it got after Lacker's comments. Though Lacker isn't a voting member of the Fed's rate-setting committee in 2011 and is widely considered hawkish, his comments still carry some weight, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "He's not a voting member, but he certainly has a voice," said Jeffrey Young, head of North American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . "If he's expressing it, there's probably others" who feel the same way among Fed members.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Australian dollar continued to recoup its gains after an initial loss following news of the Chinese rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Perceptions about the health of the Chinese economy can often dictate strength in Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because Australia's economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are heavily reliant on exporting raw materials to China. So a slowdown in China would spill over and brake \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy as well.\par \par \uc2 Egypt's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to strengthen the Egyptian pound. The pound had hit a six-year low against the dollar as ongoing civil unrest led investors to flee Egyptian financial markets.\par \par \uc2 -By Stephen L. Bernard, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-4528; stephen.bernard@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Neil Shah contributed to this article. [ 02-08-11 1703ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110208e728000dt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
