\par\par \b \uc2 Australia, NZ dlrs rapped by rising yen; bonds surge\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2010\par 23:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Hurt by rising yen, investors bet on no Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Kiwi weighed down by finance company failure\par \par \uc2 * NZ debt, Aussie bond futures rally despite upbeat data\par \par \uc2 By Adrian Bathgate and Koh Gui Qing\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars fell steadily against the yen on Tuesday as investors, undeterred by the Bank of Japan's recent policy easing, resumed bets on a rising Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Weak Asian stocks further dented demand for the pair [MARKETS/AS], overshadowing upbeat economic data from Australia. The New Zealand dollar took an additional hit from news that a small New Zealand lender had failed. [ID:nWLF004794]\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the Australian dollar fell to 75.06 <AUDJPY=R>, from 76.37 seen here late Monday. The New Zealand dollar dropped to 58.95 <NZDJPY=R>, from Monday's 60.43.\par \par \uc2 Traders said they wanted to bet on a rising yen as they thought Tokyo was reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan eased policy on Monday by expanding a cheap funding programme, but the market thought the move was futile in curbing the yen, or pulling Japan out of deflation.\par \par \uc2 "It just gives traders the green light to keep buying the yen without the threat of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said David Scutt, a trader at \uc2 Arab Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A ream of Australian data that pointed to a buoyant economy initially offered some support, but those gains were ceded towards the end of the trading session. [ID:nSGE67T08A]\par \par \uc2 Australian bond futures surged further, taking the three-year contract to a fresh 13-month peak. Three-year bond futures <YTTc1> were up 0.10 points at 95.70, while ten-year futures <YTCc1> jumped 0.07 points to 95.235.\par \par \uc2 Against the U.S. dollar, the Australian dollar eased to $0.8900 <AUD=D4>, down from the day's high of $0.8955 and Monday's $0.8981.\par \par \uc2 Near-term support for the Australian dollar was seen at $0.8870, the 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracements of its recent ascent on the hourly chart.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar <NZD=D4> retreated to $0.7020, from $0.7105 late on Monday and opening levels about $0.7080.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was weighed down in local trade by the receivership of South Canterbury Finance, one of the country's largest non-bank lenders which provides finance to the economically important agriculture sector.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi lost about half a cent and interest rates <0#NBB:> rallied, as markets bet the move would be another factor prompting the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to keep interest rates on hold said Tim Kelleher, CBA vice president of institutional banking and markets.\par \par \uc2 "The market's assuming the Reserve Bank won't tighten on the back of this, which has been negative for the kiwi," Kelleher said.\par \par \uc2 Market pricing for a hike on Sept. 16 has halved to 12 percent, from 24 percent on Monday and about 80 percent immediately after the July 29 rate rise. <CSRBNZ=CSAU>\par \par \uc2 Data on Tuesday confirmed the patchy nature of the recovery with building consents posting their second month of gains during July, boosted by a jump in apartments. [ID:nWEL004152]\par \par \uc2 An economic research group said earlier on Tuesday that the economy is slowing and would benefit from a pause in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate rise cycle into next year. [ID:nSGE67T0KV]\par \par \uc2 The NZ debt <0#NZTSY=> also rallied, with yields as much as two basis points firmer.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BONDS (UPDATE2)|LANGEN|Table|ND|ABN|D|M|RBN|AUF|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100902e68u001st\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
47
