\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: China Trade Gap Bad News For AUD\b0\par\par\uc2 1,198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 09:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0856 GMT [Dow Jones] China's warning of a $8B trade deficit in March may reduce the chances of it being named a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator by the US or having to let the CNY appreciate. But, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 , it also suggests the country is now more likely to concentrate on tightening policy domestically - i.e. hiking rates. This, the bank notes, "could potentially have a more negative impact on the commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." It is looking for the AUD to come back under pressure, with AUD/USD targeting the 0.9085 low seen Monday. The pair is now at 0.9159. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0855 GMT [Dow Jones] Swiss National Bank President Philipp Hildebrand's comments that further CHF appreciation may trigger Swiss deflation suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is close to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the franc's gains, says \uc2 National \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank\uc2 . "There has been a slight shift in emphasis, and the market is wrong to assume the SNB won't do anything concrete," says strategist Gavin Friend. "It will learn its lesson if it keeps goading the SNB by selling EUR/CHF," he says. EUR/CHF now at 1.4339. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP lower late, weighed by profit taking, inflows from overseas Filipino workers as most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced against USD; pair at 45.59 from 45.68 late Monday, volume heavy. Pair likely to stay within 45.45-45.70 range as market seeks fresh leads, says local bank trader. "There's no reason for the market to go up or down, but it would be logical to go short (on the dollar) and wait for remittances to come," adds trader. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Japan February exports likely rose 47.3% on year, buoyed by growing demand in Asia, according to average forecast of economists surveyed by Dow Jones. Such result would top January's 40.9% rise; would also likely keep trade balance solidly in surplus for month, as recovery in imports expected to continue lagging due to still sluggish domestic demand, analysts say. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones, Nikkei on average expect trade balance to log Y550 billion surplus. Trade data due at 2350 GMT. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] The Turkish lira is weaker as USD appreciates against EUR. USD/TRY trades at 1.5445 from 1.5430 Monday. Meanwhile bonds are stronger in line with gains in European bourses. The benchmark November 16, 2011 bond trades at 9.10% from 9.14% Monday. Analysts forecast TRY to trade between 1.5380 and 1.5560 and the benchmark bond to trade between 9.07% and 9.15%, in the short term. (IHA)\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT [Dow Jones] With speculative EUR shorts having been reduced notably over the past week and USD shorts increased, the positioning of speculative investors no longer presents an obstacle to a further EUR/USD fall, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . This will likely imply a further test of the lower end of EUR/USD's range at 1.3430, says the bank. EUR/USD now at 1.3515. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0828 GMT [Dow Jones] Nordea sees better value in the Dutch 4.5% July 2017 bond than in the 3.50% July 2014 bond, both on auction Tuesday. Says the July 2017 bond looks cheap on the Dutch asset swap spread curve, while it is offering a slight pickup over French peer OAT 3.75% April 2017. Separately, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  sees particularly good value in buying the July 2014 bond out of its September 2014-dated Finnish peer. With past Dutch auctions having gone well, \uc2 KBC Bank\uc2  says it has no reason to expect a different outcome of the up to EUR2 billion auction. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0828 GMT [Dow Jones] India 5-year overnight indexed swap turns up, but shorter end still trading lower from Monday's close; 1-year OIS at 4.92%/4.95% vs 4.93%/4.96% Monday while 5-year swap at 6.81%/6.86% after falling to 6.74%/6.78% vs 6.78%/6.82% last close. "Initially there was good receiving in the market. But then some foreign banks were seen paying heavily in the farther end," says dealer with state-run bank. Adds, market to remain in range this week (5-year in 6.75%-6.85% band) and make fresh move after release of April-September government borrowing plan March 29. (anant.kala@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts move lower ahead of UK inflation data Tuesday. CPI is expected to fall to 3.2% from January's 3.5%, but to remain above the level at which BOE Governor King will be required to pen another letter to Chancellor Darling. Inflation expectations were mixed at the last MPC meeting, with some voicing a concern of higher inflation risks. However, former MPC member Blanchflower believes deflationary pressures will be more of a worry in the future especially if government investment is cut back too early in the recovery phase. CPI is due at 0930 GMT, together with mortgage lending and approvals data while CBI retail sales is due at 1100 GMT. The gilt yield curve is unchanged on the day, with the 2-year/10-year benchmark spread at +291.5 bps. The June gilt futures contract is currently down 0.05 on the day at 115.44. The 10-year benchmark gilt down 0.02 on the day at 98.689, yielding 3.917%. (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR flat late at 3.3200; trader with local bank-backed brokerage says pair traded in tight 3.3170-3.3250 range, volumes thin, for most of day in absence of fresh leads. Tips 3.3100-3.3300 range tomorrow. OSK Research technical analyst Shin Kao Jack says USD will continue to drift downwards vs MYR until "downtrend channel" is violated. Tips immediate support at 3.2900-3.2700 levels, then 3.2100; resistance at 3.3300, then 3.3600. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0822 GMT [Dow Jones] The thought of running long GBP/USD positions through Tuesday's UK data run was obviously too much for some, as the spot falls one cent from its Asian session high of 1.5110. The UK data slate kicks off with February CPI and BBA Mortgages at 0930 GMT, and ends with the March CBI distributive trends survey at 1100 GMT. GBP/USD now trades at 1.5015. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0815 GMT [Dow Jones] The scope for further EUR losses is growing as hopes for an early resolution to Greece's debt problems fade, says Nicholas Hastings in \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Focus. Chances are that negotiations will now drag on until the bitter end with a rescue package emerging in one form or another only when Greece is on the brink of default. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com) [ 03-23-10 0456ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100323e63n0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
