\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For March 15\b0\par\par\uc2 1,910 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 08:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =JAPAN UPS ECON VIEW FOR 1ST TIME SINCE JULY; DEFLATION LINGERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's government raised its assessment of the economy for the first time in eight months in March, but emphasized that the risk of prolonged deflation choking off the nation's nascent recovery still lingers. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN CONSUMER SENTIMENT IMPROVES, BUT OUTLOOK UNCLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese consumers became less pessimistic on the nation's economy in February due to better income and employment conditions, data showed Monday, prompting the government to upgrade its assessment of consumer sentiment and easing concerns that Japan could fall back into recession. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN MOF NODA WANTS APPROPRIATE, FLEXIBLE BOJ ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior Japanese finance ministry official kept up the pressure Monday on the Bank of Japan, calling for "appropriate and flexible" action to support the nation's economy ahead of a two-day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meeting starting Tuesday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN FINANCE MINISTRY TO RAISE HOUSING TAX TO CURB PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to introduce a progressive housing tax to curb prices in the property sector, Deputy Minister of Finance Chang Sheng-ford said Monday. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DJ DATA SNAP: INDIA WPI UP 9.89% ON YEAR IN FEBRUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale inflation accelerated to 9.89% in February from 8.56% in January, the government said Monday. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WORLD BANK: PHILIPPINES 2010 GDP FORECAST RAISED TO 3.5% FROM 3.1% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The World Bank has upgraded its growth forecast for the Philippines this year to 3.5% from 3.1%, and projects gross domestic product to expand next year at 3.8%, helped by the stronger global economy, increasing deployment of Filipino workers overseas and robust public spending, the latest issue of the bank's Philippines Quarterly Update showed Monday. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA EDEY SAYS BANK LOAN LOSSES HAVE PEAKED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Loan losses for Australian banks arising from the global economic downturn have peaked and financial conditions are strong and improving, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malcolm Edey\f28 \uc2 \f2 , assistant governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , on Monday. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA HOPING FOR COMPREHENSIVE TRANS-PACIFIC DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's center-left Labor government is hoping talks over a Trans-Pacific Partnership, which began in Melbourne Monday, will be a chance to seek a more comprehensive regional agreement than those negotiated in various bilateral free trade deals, including one Canberra reached with the U.S. in 2005. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVERNMENT: NO TIMING SET FOR CONDUCTING EXIT STRATEGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Monday that no specific timing has been set for an exit from the government's current accommodative economic policies. (published 0458 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANCO SANTANDER\f28 \uc2 \f2  LIKELY WON'T OFFER A$ DEBT NEAR TERM -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  will likely not issue debt in Australian dollars in the near term despite holding talks with investors last week, people familiar with the matter said Monday. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S ADELAIDE AIRPORT MAY BUY BACK A$264M DEBT - LEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adelaide Airport Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is in talks with investors about a possible buy back of existing maturing debt in exchange for new bonds, a lead said Monday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRANSURBAN: TO ISSUE A$250M SECURED FIXED RATE MEDIUM TERM NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toll roads operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transurban Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it will issue A$250 million of 2014 fixed rate notes, at 180 basis points over swap. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AMMB UNIT PLANS TO SELL UP TO MYR2.5 BLN NOTES - DOCUMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ambank Bhd, a unit of publicly listed \f28 \uc2 \f2 AMMB Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , plans to sell up to MYR2.5 billion of notes, with the option of upsizing the issue to MYR3.0 billion, according to an information memorandum seen by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI PM: WON'T DISSOLVE PARLIAMENT AS DEMANDED BY PROTESTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said Monday that he won't dissolve parliament and call new elections as demanded by protesters loyal to fugitive ex-premier Thaksin Shinawatra. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: TAIWAN IS PUTTING RATE HIKES ON THE BACKBURNER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Targeted steps taken by Taiwan authorities to prevent potential asset bubbles in the property market suggest the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely delay any interest rate hikes until the third quarter at the earliest. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: THE NIMBY APPROACH TO GLOBAL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Premier Wen Jiabao's weekend comments on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflect the NIMBY approach being taken around the globe--and why major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy change remains an unlikely near-term prospect. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: RATE HIKES, RECOVERY TO DRIVE MALAYSIAN RINGGIT RALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Malaysian ringgit will likely rise further against the dollar in coming months, driven by expectations of quick interest rate hikes and continued strength of China's economy, which is pushing up demand for Malaysian exports like palm oil. (published 0427 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DLR/YEN OPTIONS DOWN; FOMC, BOJ MEETINGS AWAITED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell in Tokyo Monday as investors avoided active trading ahead of the policy-setting meetings of the Japanese and U.S. central banks later this week, the outcomes of which are far from clear. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHONGQING WATER GROUP IPO TO RAISE UP TO CNY3.49 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chongqing Water Group Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise up to CNY3.49 billion from an initial public offering, after setting an indicative price range for the IPO of CNY6.48 to CNY6.98 a share. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOOK WOO GROUP SEEKS UP TO US$212 MLN IN HK IPO -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese waste-paper management services provider and recycled paper products producer Fook Woo Group Holdings Ltd. is seeking to raise up to US$212 million in a Hong Kong initial public offering, a person familiar with the situation said Sunday. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORMER ADVISER AT MACQUARIE GROUP PLEADS GUILTY TO MARKET MANIPULATION -ASIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former adviser at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has pleaded guilty to illegally manipulating the price of collapsed software firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bill Express Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Australia's corporate regulator said Monday. (published 2351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KUMHO LIFE INSURANCE PLANS PUBLIC LISTING IN 2012 - CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kumho Life Insurance plans a public listing in 2012, the firm's chief executive said Monday. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: QUESTIONS ARISE IN PRIUS CASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An investigation of the Toyota Prius involved in a dramatic incident on a California highway last week is raising questions about the driver's version of the event. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HUTCHISON TELECOM\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAY DELIST IN HK MAY 25 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Telecommunications Ltd. plans to delist from the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on May 25 and from the New York Stock Exchange on June 4, if parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hutchison Whampoa Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . gains approval from a Cayman Islands court and shareholders to take the telecom services provider private for US$545 million, the two companies said Sunday. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: WUHAN IRON BUYS STAKE IN LIBERIA MINE FOR $68.46 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wuhan Iron & Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's third-largest steelmaker, said Monday it has acquired a 60% stake in an iron ore mine in Liberia for $68.46 million from the China-Africa Development Fund, whose funds mainly come from China Development Bank Corp. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: CHINA SETS H-P INQUIRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's product-quality agency said it is investigating complaints from a small number of Chinese consumers about \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s handling of flaws in some of its personal computers. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIMB THAI BANK BOARD OKS BT INSURANCE SALE FOR THB392 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CIMB Thai Bank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday its board has approved the disposal of a 99.99% stake in BT Insurance Co. Ltd. to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ayudhya Insurance PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  for THB392 million . (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAL-COMP ELECTRONICS TO SPEND UP TO S$25 MLN TO BUY AVAPLAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cal-comp Electronics PCL said Monday it expects to spend as much as S$25 million, or THB584.4 million, to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Avaplas Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arrk Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VISHAL RETAIL\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S LENDERS AGREE TO TPG TAKEOVER - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A group of lenders to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vishal Retail Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have approved a plan under which U.S. private equity firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 TPG Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will take over the debt-laden Indian retailer, a person with direct knowledge of the development said. (published 0352 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY DOWN: TIGHTENING CONCERNS HURT CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Monday, with shares in China and Hong Kong weighed down by lingering worries over fresh monetary tightening measures from Beijing. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRADE MINISTER REITERATES WON'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN IRON ORE TALKS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Trade Minister Simon Crean on Monday reiterated that the Australian government won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in iron ore price negotiations between companies including \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and BHP Billiton and Chinese buyers. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS:CHINA METALS PRODUCERS SEEK CONSOLIDATION, OVERSEAS ACQUISITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As China's sprawling non-ferrous metals industry gets moving on a government-mandated consolidation within the sector, the country's largest corporations are also actively seeking mining projects in Afghanistan, Congo, Tanzania and Zambia, among the others. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BHP BILLITON SAYS MAJOR COKING COAL PORT STILL CLOSED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-03-10 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its key Hay Point coking coal export terminal near Mackay in Queensland state remains closed for a fifth day due to bad weather conditions. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EL NINO,DROUGHT AFFECTING SE ASIA SPRING RICE CROP -FAO OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An El Nino weather phenomenon and accompanying drought is affecting the spring rice harvest in Southeast Asian countries, a senior official at the Food and Agriculture Organization said. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWMONT SEES STRONG 2010 CHINA GOLD DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S.-based gold producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Newmont Mining Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that Chinese demand for gold bullion will remain strong this year, despite historically high prices for the metal. (published 0325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CNPC: SIGNED AGREEMENT WITH YUNNAN PROVINCE ON CBM DEVELOPMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the nation's top oil and gas producer, signed a strategic cooperation framework agreement last Friday with the Yunnan provincial government on developing and utilizing coal bed methane, the company said on its Web site Monday. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MALAYSIA JANUARY NATURAL RUBBER OUTPUT AT 16-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's natural rubber production in January rose 48% from a year earlier to a 16-month high of 108,892 metric tons, as favorable weather boosted output. End-month stocks also rose, but exports and imports surged with support from Chinese demand. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN SCIENTISTS PIN GLOBAL WARMING ON HUMANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A trend of rising average global temperatures is almost certainly the result of human activity, two of the Australian government's leading climate science agencies said Monday. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA TO SET UP RESEARCH BODIES TO MONITOR CLIMATE CHANGE - MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is setting up a network of research bodies and scientists to gather climate change data in a bid to bolster the country's negotiating stand at the global level and counter what it sees as a "propaganda science" of developed countries, federal Environment Minister Jairam Ramesh said. (published 0518 GMT) [ 15-03-10 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100315e63f000ew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
