\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,112 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S RBA STUNS MARKETS WITH RATES ON-HOLD DECISION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  stunned financial markets Tuesday with a decision to leave its cash rate target unchanged at 3.75%, saying it needs time to assess the effects of rate rises in late 2009 and hefty increases in bank lending margins. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OECD URGES CHINA TO RELY MORE ON INTEREST RATES IN MONETARY POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development on Tuesday urged China to increase the flexibility of the yuan exchange rate and rely more on interest rates as a monetary policy tool over time, as Beijing has begun to withdraw the stimulus measures introduced late 2008 to combat the effects of the global financial crisis. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN 4Q BUSINESS EXPECTATIONS INDEX RISES TO 62.6 PTS VS 59.3 PTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business expectations rose to a record high in the fourth quarter, according to a private sector survey published Tuesday. (published 0025 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND WAGE GROWTH LOWEST IN NEARLY 9 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's wage growth remained weak in the fourth quarter and the annual growth slipped to its lowest level in nearly nine years with economists forecasting only moderate wage increases this year as the economy gradually recovers. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES RISE TO RECORD IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rebounded to an all-time high in January, propelled by investment gains, the retrieval of dollar loans and suspected dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 AUSTRALIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM: AS GLOBAL ECONOMY RECOVERS, INTEREST RATES WILL CHANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Prime Minister Kevin Rudd said Tuesday that the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made clear for some time that as the global economy recovers, interest rates will be changed from their record low levels. (published 2121 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA SAYS PROTECTIONISM HURTS CHINA-U.S. TRADE TIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China says that the U.S. has increasingly fallen back on protectionism since the onset of the global financial crisis, which has affected trade relations between the two countries. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN PM HATOYAMA: TO CONTINUE TO WORK WITH BOJ VS DEFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Yukio Hatoyama made a renewed pledge Tuesday to work closely with the Bank of Japan to get rid of deflation that is weighing on the country's economic recovery. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S KAN: WANT BOJ TO ACT PROPERLY, FLEXIBLY FOR ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister Tuesday continued to call for the Bank of Japan to act properly and flexibly to help the nation's economy grow, but he refrained from saying exactly what kinds of steps he wants the bank to undertake. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE OFFICIAL: FIRST-QUARTER GROWTH MAY EXCEED 2.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippines economic growth in the first quarter of the year could exceed 2.6%, the lower end of a government target set for the year, as exports are expected to recover, a senior finance official said Tuesday. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBNZ TO DECREASE LIQUIDITY RISK IN NON-BANK DEPOSIT-TAKING SECTOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand released a consultation paper Tuesday on policy options for liquidity requirements for the non-bank deposit-taking sector. (published 2120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN INVESTORS BOUGHT BULK OF RCBC'S $250M 5-YEAR BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian investors took the lion's share of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rizal Commercial Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . 's $250-million five-year bonds sold late Monday, a person familiar with the deal said Tuesday. (published 0203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES TREASURY REJECTS BIDS FOR NOVEMBER 2016 BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine government rejected all bids for a treasury bond due November 2016 at an auction Tuesday as the treasury deemed that the yields banks sought were too high. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM'S $1 BLN BOND SALE RAISES NATIONAL DEBT TO ABOVE 30% OF GDP - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's $1 billion international bond sale last month has raised the country's national debt to above 30% of gross domestic product, state media said Tuesday, citing Deputy Minister of Finance Tran Xuan Ha. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA TO LIMIT GAINS FROM PUBLIC SERVICE CHARGES TO STABLILIZE PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government aims to maintain price stability by limiting any potential gains from public service charges, such as for electricity, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Tuesday. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT POLL SUPPORT FALLS; CLIMATE SHOWDOWN LOOMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's center-left Labor government has suffered a big fall in voter support as it faces growing pressure over its plan to cap the nation's greenhouse-gas emissions, according to a voter poll published Tuesday. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA WATCHING FOR POSSIBLE NORTH KOREA MISSILE TESTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's military was watching on Tuesday for any North Korean missile tests after the communist state banned shipping from several more coastal zones in its territory. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TATA SONS PLANS TO RAISE INR10 BILLION VIA DEBENTURES - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Sons Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to raise INR10 billion by selling non-convertible debentures, The Economic Times newspaper reported Tuesday, citing a person close to the development. (published 0328 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK PM: WILL DO 'EVERYTHING NECESSARY' TO END FISCAL CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek Prime Minister George Papandreou pledged Monday to do "everything necessary" to pull the country out of a fiscal hole that has hurt its standing on the financial markets. (published 2024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MEXICO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHIEF TO WORK CLOSELY WITH GOVERNMENT - FT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mexico \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new chief will cooperate closely with the government during his six-year tenure, which could cause investor jitters regarding the bank's independence, the Financial Times reported on its Web site Monday, citing an interview with Agust\u237\'00\'EDn Carstens. (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: KOREAN WON TO STRENGTHEN FURTHER, LEAD ASIAN RALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even as the South Korean won keeps dropping against the U.S. dollar, signs are mounting that a won rally is just around the corner. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: YEN OPTIONS DOWN AS US DATA BOOST RISK APPETITE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell in Tokyo on Tuesday as stronger-than-expected overnight U.S. data prompted dealers to bet the dollar won't fall sharply, at least for the days ahead, although options prices may not fall much further. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED WATCH: EMERGENCY EFFORTS WINDING DOWN AMID MARKET APPROVAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In with a bang, out with a whimper. And so it goes for a series of emergency lending programs hatched by the Federal Reserve over the course of the worst financial crisis since the Great Depression. (published 2014 GMT) [ 02-02-10 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100202e622000hj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
