\par\par \b \uc2 Australian Dlr Higher Late As Greenback Slips Further\b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 06:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Rates At 0535 GMT \par                            Latest       Change \par  AUD/USD                   0.7053       +0.4% \par  AUD/JPY                   61.88         0.0% \par  5.75% June. 11, 2011      3.125%       -0.02 \par  6.00% Feb. 15, 2017       3.90%        -0.0675 \par  10-Yr Spread To U.S.      +195 bps     -20 bps \par  SFE Mar 3-Year Futures    96.635       +0.015 \par  SFE Mar 10-Year Futures   95.95        +0.10 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar held above US$0.70 near a two-month high late Thursday as the greenback's status as a safehaven asset was brought further into question.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Australian bond yield curve has continued to flatten as longer-dated yields tracked their U.S. counterparts down to new record lows.\par \par \uc2 While firming on the U.S. dollar weakness, the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has severely underperformed the euro, which has recently soared to a two-and-a-half month high of US$1.4452.\par \par \uc2 "The Aussie is up against the U.S. but the global outlook for growth hasn't changed that much so that's why we're lagging on some of these crosses," ANZ senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Tony Morriss said.\par \par \uc2 At 0535 GMT, the Australian dollar was trading at US$0.7053, up from US$0.7022 late Wednesday. In the Asian session it hit US$0.7079, its highest reading since Oct. 14. Against the Japanese yen, it was trading at Y61.88, down from Y61.895.\par \par \uc2 Morriss doesn't believe the recent U.S. dollar weakness will become a more permanent trend with the market focus expected to shift to the strong possibility of a narrowing of the U.S. and Eurozone interest rate differentials.\par \par \uc2 "I think the U.S. dollar can regain some ground - when the market does start to focus on European weakness there is some scope for the euro to lose some momentum," he said.\par \par \uc2 The VIX volatility index has also retreated below 50 for the first time since Oct. 3 lending some support to high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, any resulting advances in commodities prices have been very modest, tempering the Australian dollar's gains.\par \par \uc2 John Kyriakopoulos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with nabCapital, believes the Australian dollar is poised for a recovery back toward US$0.79 in 2009.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar has likely bottomed out at US$0.60, he said. This is helped by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the low US$0.60s last month indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being fundamentally cheap around these levels.\par \par \uc2 "While Chinese economic growth has slowed sharply recently, a massive spending boost and rapid interest rate cuts will support stronger growth in the second half of 2009," Kyriakopoulos said.\par \par \uc2 "This should ensure that Australia's commodity prices and terms of trade remain well above their long-term averages, supporting the Australian dollar above its long-term average of US$0.72."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Philadelphia Federal Reserve's manufacturing index for December is due later Thursday. Economists expect the index's business activity reading to have fallen to -40 from -39.3 in November. This could give some direction to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Australian bond futures were stronger with 10-year March futures contracts surging 10 ticks to a new record high of 95.95 and the three year futures contract rising 1.5 ticks to 96.635.\par \par \uc2 The spread between the implied three- and 10-year bond yields has fallen to 69 basis points from a peak of 114 basis points earlier this week.Shorter-dated yields have risen on reduced domestic interest rate cut expectations while longer-dated yields have been pushed down by recent news the Fed is likely to move to a quantitative easing monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Sam Holmes, Dow Jones Newswires; \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 61-2-8235-2964; samuel.holmes@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Data provided by Reuters) [ 18-12-08 0548GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1054 22765 4109   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081218e4ci00053\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
