\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (RBA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in late October to buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it collapsed to 60 cents amid global market turmoil. It has since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again around $0.6350. [nSYU005568]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Analysts said the extent of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed its commitment to keeping any fall orderly and might make bears wary of shorting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too far, too fast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Aussie was hovering around $0.6394, having found support at $0.6360 <AUD=>. It had been as high as $0.6597 offshore before U.S. equities sank. The S&P <.SPX> ended down 6 percent on fears of a deep recession [.N]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Aussie also down at 61.25 yen <AUDJPY=R>, and away from a 63.86 peak in New York. Renewed flight to the perceived safety of the Japanese yen has lifted it across the board.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Destruction of equity wealth and more dire U.S. data [nN19322315] reinforced expectations of more aggressive rate cuts from the RBA, boosting bill futures <0#YBA:>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * RBA Governor Glenn Stevens late Wednesday said Australia had ample scope to move to an expansionary policy [nSYD166219], both through interest rates and fiscal spending.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The market is already pricing in a rate cut of at least 75 basis points in the 5.25 percent cash rate at its December meeting, and further drastic easing to 3.5 percent next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Three-year bond futures <YTTc1> climbed 0.055 points to 96.310, having earlier touched a record high of 96.350, while the 10-year contract <YTCc1> added 0.06 to 95.215.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Treasuries were even stronger as U.S. consumer prices fell a steep 1 percent in October [nTOPMACRO] and the Fed signalled a willingness to ease again [nFEDAHEAD].\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Two-year Treasury yields fell to their lowest since 1976 while the spread between Australian and U.S. 10-year yields widened out to 146 basis points. (Reporting by Wayne Cole, Editing by Mark Bendeich)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-BONDS/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NOON|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081123e4bk0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
