\par\par \b \uc2 Australian Dlr Higher Late, RBA Steps In, G20 Summit Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 491 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2008\par 06:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Rates At 0450 GMT \par                            Latest       Change \par  AUD/USD                   0.6562        +2.7% \par  AUD/JPY                   63.665        +4.2% \par  5.75% June. 11, 2011      3.823%        +0.08 \par  6.00% Feb. 15, 2017       4.825         +0.085 \par  10-Yr Spread To U.S.      +107 bps      -27 bps \par  SFE Dec 3-Year Futures    96.145        -0.07 \par  SFE Dec 10-Year Futures   95.985        -0.095 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--A surge on Wall Street lifted risk appetite in Asia Friday, sending the Australian dollar sharply higher and cooling red hot interest rate futures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Helping the \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's bounce was another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York trading.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to give details on what level it bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but local traders pinpoint the US$0.6350 area as the trigger for buying. This area also marked its overnight low.\par \par \uc2 Having rallied hard early after the Dow Jones Industrial Average closed 6.7% higher, the local unit tailed off as traders await the outcome of this weekend's Group of 20 industrial and developing nations meeting in Washington D.C.\par \par \uc2 Although few concrete decisions are expected from the meeting, market analysts say any joint statement flagging coordinated action of some kind could impact \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 At 0450 GMT, the Australian dollar was trading at US$0.6562, up from US$0.6392 late Thursday, having hit a low of US$0.6342. Against the Japanese yen, it was trading at Y63.665, up from Y61.09.\par \par \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  Strategist Patrick Bennett said although the unwinding of carry trade positions is now largely complete, the risks for the local unit remain firmly to the downside.\par \par \uc2 "At this stage people are happy to sell current account deficit \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " such as the Australian dollar, Bennett said.\par \par \uc2 Still, given the market has already priced in a raft of expected bad news, there is some potential for the Australian dollar to gain, ABN AMRO Strategist Greg Gibbs said, but added any turnaround won't be sustained.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe there's scope for it to reverse some of that weakness purely on technical grounds rather than any sentiment that things have really changed."\par \par \uc2 The December three-year bond futures contract fell 7 ticks to 96.145. The December 10-year futures contract fell 9.5 ticks to 95.985.\par \par \uc2 "I think you've got to be bullish bonds," ICAP Economist Adam Carr said.\par \par \uc2 "The data flow is going to continue to be negative - what we saw in U.S. equities and the Aussie market is just a little bit too optimistic and we'll see a bit of a correction, certainly into the early part of next week."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    -By Enda Curran, Dow Jones Newswires; \par    61-2-8235-2958; enda.curran@dowjones.com \par  \par    (Data provided by Reuters) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-11-08 0519GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1054 22765 4109   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081114e4be0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
