\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Australia RBA Bought AUD To Boost Liquidity Offshore\b0\par\par\uc2 By Enda Curran and Samuel Holmes   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2008\par 05:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed Friday it again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the Australian dollar, stepping in during New York trading, a spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been amongst the biggest victims of the global financial and economic crisis, slumping almost 40% since hitting post float record highs in July.\par \par \uc2 The RBA said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to improve liquidity, but wouldn't give any detail on the levels it bought at.\par \par \uc2 It's the second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having bought the Australian dollar during New York trading Wednesday, and follows a flurry of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 Traders speculate the RBA has been targeting the US$0.6350 level as a trigger to step in, though the RBA's official line has always been it doesn't draw any 'lines in the sand', and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  solely to smooth gappy price action.\par \par \uc2 During New York trading, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced sharply from a low of US$0.6348 to US$0.6694, before tailing off again in the Asia session.\par \par \uc2 ABN Amro Strategist Greg Gibbs was skeptical the RBA's actions sparked the recovery, more likely the sudden surge in U.S. stocks. "I would say 99% of the bounce was on the back of the turn in equities. I would say they prevented it going much below U$0.6350."\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones industrial average finished 6.7% higher, having recovered from an intraday fall of 300 points.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong-based \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  strategist Patrick Bennett said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely remain alert to further sharp falls in the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We'll continue to see them, but I don't think they're trying to set any level where they want to act," Bennett said.\par \par \uc2 -By Enda Curran, Dow Jones Newswires;\par \par \uc2 61-2-8235-2958; enda.curran@dowjones.com [ 14-11-08 0401GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081114e4be00057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
