\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen plunges across the board as stocks surge\b0\par\par\uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 03:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen posts biggest one-day fall since euro's launch\par \par \uc2 * Stock rebound worldwide spurs tentative risk appetite\par \par \uc2 * Bank of Japan may cut interest rates-Nikkei report (Updates prices, adds quotes, changes byline)\par \par \uc2 By Wanfeng Zhou\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 28 (Reuters) - The yen slumped across the board on Tuesday, recording its worst one-day decline against the euro ever as a sharp rebound in global equities sparked a tentative recovery in risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also posted its biggest daily fall versus the U.S. dollar since 1974, according to Reuters data. The yen extended its losses after Japan's leading business newspaper said the Bank of Japan is mulling an interest rate cut to support its sagging economy.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks ended sharply higher, with the Dow Jones industrial average surging almost 11 percent as investors scooped up beaten-down shares amid optimism the Federal Reserve and other central banks will cut interest rates further.\par \par \uc2 The move followed gains in European and Asian equities overnight, boosting the euro and the Australian dollar, two of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  most battered versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 "We're seeing a reversal of what's been a very strong trend over the past several weeks," said Stephen Malyon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto. The BoJ story "added to the bearish momentum in the yen from yesterday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumors and also the relatively positive day in the equity market.\par \par \uc2 "Now whether that sustains itself is still the big question. We've seen a number of rebounds in the equity market unravel within the following one or two days. There is still the big question about whether today's rebound is sustainable," he added.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment remains nervous and some analysts said the stock markets' relief rally and the yen's fall may prove temporary as fears of a prolonged global recession should keep investors in risk-averse mode.\par \par \uc2 In late trading in New York, the dollar jumped 5.4 percent to 97.75 yen <JPY=>, moving away from a 13-year low just above 90 yen struck on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The euro rallied more than 7 percent to 124.29 yen <EURJPY=>, its biggest one-day move since the launch of the 15-nation \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999. The euro hit a 6-1/2 year low of 113.79 yen on Friday, according to electronic trading platform EBS.\par \par \uc2 The euro also rose 2 percent to $1.2715 after hitting a 2-1/2-year low earlier. European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet on Monday said the bank could cut rates from the current 3.75 percent at its policy meeting next week.\par \par \uc2 The Fed is seen easing the fed funds rate -- currently at 1.50 percent -- by at least half a percentage point at the end of its two-day meeting on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We'll need to see what the Fed does tomorrow and of course how markets overnight react," said Brian Dolan, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .com in Bedminster, New Jersey. "Sentiment is still extremely fragile. But the process of bottoming and process of stabilizing is underway."\par \par \uc2 BOJ RATE CUT\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan is considering cutting interest rates by a quarter-percentage point to shore up a sagging economy battered by a strong yen and declining equity prices, the Nikkei business newspaper reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is leaning toward reducing its current 0.5 percent target rate for the unsecured overnight call money rate to 0.25 percent, Nikkei said, without citing sources. For more, see [ID:nN28531832].\par \par \uc2 "The BoJ story as well as today's stock rally are contributing to the yen's woes," said Ashraf Laidi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CMC Markets U.S.\par \par \uc2 "A BoJ rate cut would also be more effective in stabilizing yen strength than mere \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if the rate cut is accompanied by Fed easing and overt yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- if the needs arises," Laidi said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the yen's fall has eased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks from the Bank of Japan to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for trade purposes, but remained a threat given the surge in volatility.\par \par \uc2 The yen's one-month implied volatility <JPY1MO=> hit more than 39 percent on Monday, Reuters data showed, and while it eased on Tuesday, it remained elevated at 32 percent.\par \par \uc2 Distressed stock prices and the yen's rapid rise succeeded in getting the Group of Seven nations' attention as they warned against excessive yen volatility on Monday. That was seen as opening the way for the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if warranted.\par \par \uc2 In other trading, the Australian dollar climbed 6.9 percent against the U.S. dollar to US$0.6435 <AUD=> after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a third straight day. The Aussie dollar has lost more than 35 percent against the greenback since peaking in July. (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 10)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|UKI|Z|CANT|AUF|ABX|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081028e4as000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw83\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1245\pichgoal600
