\par\par \b \uc2 Australia Market Report of October 28: Not Volatile As Expected\b0\par\par\uc2 952 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 03:15\par \uc2 ABN Newswire\par \uc2 ABNENG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2008.  Asia Business News Pty Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 Sydney, Australia, Oct 28, 2008 - (ABN Newswire) -  Overnight the US stocks continued to fall to lows with sell-off on the close, and Dow has been showing a 25 per cent loss for October so far.\par \par \uc2 The Australian sharemarket has closed at a fresh four-year low after falling more than 1% on renewed global recession fears. Investors actually had expected a much more volatile as the significant declines on Wall Street last Friday gave a negative lead to the local market. Analysts said it was not as bad as expected and the miners performed well yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The December Share Price Index futures contract on the Sydney Futures Exchange up just 2 points at 3793 in recent trading.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark S&P/ASX200 share index yesterday sank to a fresh four-year low, losing 1.6%, or 60.2 points to 3809 points.\par \par \uc2 The broader All Ordinaries index shed 63.3 points, or 1.7%, to 3768.3, the lowest close in four years.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar has opened weaker for the fifth day in a row, hitting another five-year low overnight. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) also has failed to give the Australian dollar a sustained boost, with traders reluctant to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during a time of falling commodity prices. At 7am, the Australian dollar was trading at $US0.6037/43, down from yesterday's close of $US0.6119/26.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices sank to 17-month lows during trade overnight amid rising worries that a global recession will sap energy demand, particularly in Asia where markets have plunged to 20-year lows. New York's main contract, light sweet crude for December delivery, fell 93 cents to close at $US63.22 dollars a barrel, after falling as low as $US61.30 during trade.\par \par \uc2 Key Economic Facts and Figures\par \par \uc2 A report from the Australian Council of Superannuation Investors (ACSI) shows that the average fixed pay for 69 CEOs from the biggest 100 listed companies rose 106 per cent from 2001 to 2007. The average fixed salary of the 69 CEOs surveyed rose to A$1.83 million from 1.80 million in 2006 and compares with A$888,407 in 2001.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank was forced to shore up the beleaguered Australian dollar yesterday for the second time in four days. After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday night as the dollar plunged almost US7c, the Reserve stepped in again yesterday to shield the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against speculators. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying helped the dollar to rise above US62c. But last night it plunged again on overseas markets to US60.6c.\par \par \uc2 The Australian Office of Financial Management is due to announce its latest Treasury bond tender result today, while \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2  will release its business survey for the September quarter.\par \par \uc2 M&A News\par \par \uc2 Great Australian Resources Ltd\uc2  (ASX:GAU) has entered into a strategic acquisition deal with \uc2 Sylvania Resources Ltd\uc2  (ASX:SLV) which allows Great Australian Resources to acquire three platinum projects in the northwestern limb of the Bushveld Igneous Complex in South Africa.\par \par \uc2 Floreat Forum is about to change hands as a major private investor group is conducting due diligence on it, which the troubled property company \uc2 GPT Group\uc2 (ASX:GPT) is understood to be ready to sell for about A$115 million.\par \par \uc2 Important Corporate News\par \par \uc2 Wealth manager \uc2 BT Investment Management\uc2 (ASX:BTT) has reported a $14.3 million profit from its first year of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying a strong balance sheet positions it to take advantage of growth opportunities in current dislocated markets.\par \par \uc2 Lihir Gold\uc2 (ASX:LGL) achieved record production in its third quarter, reporting 250,000 ounces, up 41 per cent on the previous quarter. In 2008, the company expects production of about 850,000 ounces, in line with its previous guidance.\par \par \uc2 Austar United Communications\uc2 (ASX:AUN) today said it was confident of 20 per cent earnings growth, as it reported deeper market penetration amid tough economic times. A statement by Austar said earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation rose to A$53 million in the September quarter, from A$46.4 million in the previous three months.\par \par \uc2 1. Related Stocks - Mid Market (12:30 AEST)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------\par Code     % Change   Volume     Turnover      Low  High\par ------------------------------------------------------\par ASX:GAU   +12.5    30,000      $1,350        4.5   4.5\par ASX:SLV   -11.33   28,253      $19,991       66.5  74\par ASX:GPT   -7.14    25,481,761  $19,669,262   75.5  79\par ASX:BTT   -3.1     25,146      $62,980       249   258\par ASX:LGL   +3.82    8,271,400   $13,571,826   161.5 167\par ASX:AUN   +4.44    670,219     $621,725      90    95\par ------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2. Top 10 ASX on Turnover - Mid Market (12:30 AEST)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------\par Code     % Change   Volume     Turnover      Low  High\par ------------------------------------------------------\par ASX:QGC   +79.68  54,174,287   $311,506,312  575   576\par ASX:BHP   +1.26   6,764,821    $173,962,233  2460  2528\par ASX:WBC   -1.55   3,879,378    $77,480,201   1962  2005\par ASX:CBA   -1.67   1,776,481  