\par\par \b \uc2 Australia's RBA Buys Australian Dollars At US$0.6125-Traders\b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 01:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar in early trading Monday, according to market participants.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the RBA bought Australian dollars at around US$0.6125, which fueled a quick rally to a high of US$0.6217.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the RBA wouldn't immediately comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0025 GMT, the Australian dollar was quoted at US$0.6184.\par \par \uc2 No detail was available on the amount spent by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, who requested anonymity, said conditions are so illiquid in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that it would not take much to give the Australian dollar a boost.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday night, when the RBA stepped in to support the Australian dollar which plunged seven US cents in one day. Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first since August 2007.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the RBA told Dow Jones Newswires earlier today that Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was designed to "add liquidity".\par \par \uc2 Against the U.S. dollar, the Australian dollar has fallen by 37% since midyear amid growing concern about the world growth outlook.\par \par \uc2 -By James Glynn; Dow Jones Newswires; 612-8235-2955; james.glynn@dowjones.com\par \p