\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 3-Asia keeps cash flowing to markets despite rally\b0\par\par\uc2 809 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2008\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Japan, Australia, Indonesia India add cash to money markets\par \par \uc2  * Dollar funds tight in Asia, cheaper in London\par \par \uc2  * N.Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eases collateral rules\par \par \uc2  * China scraps share purchase tax, buys stocks  (Repeats to more  subscribers)\par \par \uc2  By Hideyuki Sano and Yoo Choonsik\par \par \uc2  TOKYO/SEOUL, Sept 19 (Reuters) - Asia-Pacific nations kept up efforts on Friday to shield the region from the fallout of Wall Street upheaval even as stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied in response to emergency action from the world's top financial authorities.\par \par \uc2  Japan, Australia, India and Indonesia pumped over $42 billion into their money markets as cash remained hard to come by despite Thursday's unprecedented move by the U.S. Federal Reserve to make $180 billion available by to the global banking system.  The Chinese government bought shares in three of the biggest state-owned banks and ditched a tax on purchases of stocks to support its stock market.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor Masaaki Shirakawa told lawmakers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept all of its options open, when asked about the possibility of cutting its ultra-low 0.5 percent benchmark rate. His South Korean counterpart promised to act aggressively and supply enough cash to the financial system to calm markets while New Zealand relaxed rules on collateral to ease funding conditions. [ID:nWEL348670]\par \par \uc2  Asian stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied on Friday taking cue from Wall Street gains overnight following news of a U.S. Treasury plan to create a fund that would mop up toxic debt, similar to one that helped resolve the savings and loan crisis of the late 1980s.\par \par \uc2  Britain imposed a temporary ban on short selling of financial stocks on Thursday. The Wall Street Journal reported U.S.  regulators were considering a similar step and the Securities   and Exchange Commission chairman Christopher Cox told reporters he could make a statement on the issue as early as Friday.\par \par \uc2  Short selling allows investors to profit from falling prices and has helped bring Wall Street icons to their knees.\par \par \uc2  The plans offered investors a glimmer of hope for resolution to the 13-month old credit crisis that sank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , stripped \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  and \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  of their independence and triggered a $85 billion bailout of insurer AIG.\par \par \uc2  TIGHT CASH\par \par \uc2  The news helped bring down overnight dollar interbank rates in London to 2 percent, around the Fed's target.\par \par \uc2  But during the Asian day funding remained tight with banks lending dollars to each other at between 3 and 6 percent, still off a peak of 10 percent hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  "They are dealing well with an extremely difficult situation ... they may need to do more to boost liquidity and confidence," said David Mann, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered Bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  Mindful of sharp market swings in the past week and anxiety still gripping investors, officials sought to play it safe, expecting tight funding conditions would persist for some time.\par \par \uc2  Asked in parliament whether an interest rate cut by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  was a possibility, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said:\par \par \uc2  "We have no pre-determined conclusion. You just talked about an urgent rate cut. Central banks, including the BOJ, always consider all options. That's our principle."\par \par \uc2  While the world's top central banks dished out billions of dollars to grease money markets, both the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and the Fed kept their benchmark rates on hold this week and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep its rates steady too.\par \par \uc2  South Korean authorities said they would meet next week to work out ways of protecting Asia's fourth-largest economy from the impact of global markets turbulence.\par \par \uc2  "There are worries that the instability in the financial markets could hurt the real economy," Finance Minister Kang Man-soo told a meeting of senior financial officials. "The government needs to look more closely into the situation and study possible ways to minimise any impact," he said.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  pumped 3 trillion yen ($28.72 billion) into the money market for the fourth day in a row as foreign borrowers struggled to get cash and were charged much more than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 0.5 percent policy target for overnight funds.\par \par \uc2  India injected 591 billion Indian rupees ($12.75 billion) into its money market at a repo auction, in part to offset the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added A$2.03 billion ($1.6 billion) in its regular market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  repurchase agreements, while draining A$1.0 billion through a same-day \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap.    Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stepped to help in with help with little less than $500 million in six-day funds.      \par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL/POLICYMAKERS (WRAPUP 3)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080919e49j00076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
