\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie dollar under pressure despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 03:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar stayed near five-month lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, despite overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the squeeze in global credit markets saw investors dump riskier assets.   \par \par \uc2 * The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) said on Friday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets overnight in an effort to restore some liquidity to the market for the Australian dollar.   \par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been routinely selling Australian dollars in the last few years as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose. The last time it bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a net basis in a month was back in late 2001.   \par \par \uc2 * RBA Governor Glenn Stevens told lawmakers that recent developments in credit markets added uncertainty to the economic outlook, though he also said the turmoil was unlikely to dent Australian business confidence.   \par \par \uc2 * Deepening troubles in the U.S. subprime mortgage markets and a growing investor preference for safe-haven assets saw unwinding of risky carry trades escalate. Under carry trades, investors borrow in the low-yielding Japanese yen to buy high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Aussie and New Zealand dollars.   \par \par \uc2 * The Aussie slumped to its lowest since Sept. 2006 against the Japanese yen in New York trade falling as low as 87.76 yen <AUDJPY=R>, down over 22 percent since its July 20, 16-year high of 107.72 yen.   \par \par \uc2 * At 11:22 a.m. (0122 GMT), the Aussie <AUD=> was quoted at $0.7853/58/71, having fallen as far as $0.7781 in early deals, its weakest since March 9, according to Reuters data. It had slid to $0.7818 against the U.S. dollar in New York trade.   \par \par \uc2 * Australian government bonds continued to firm on Friday on safe-haven demand.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070820e38h0002p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
