\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Australia Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By V. Phani Kumar   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones) -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on the previous day, for the first time in six years, to restore liquidity, according to wire service reports.   \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens told a parliamentary hearing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a "disorderly" market.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't typically signal intentions about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of time... so I prefer not to speculate about the future," he said, according to wire service reports. "On occasion where market conditions are disorderly, we are prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time."   \par \par \uc2 Reports said the size of the RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was small.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar rose 2.7% to A$1.2937 and the Australian dollar fell 3.3% to 87.43 yen. [ 08-17-07 1200ET ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020070817e38h0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
