\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day   \b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 07:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIA-PACIFIC CENTRAL BANKS SEEK TO KEEP MARKETS LIQUID    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan pumped more cash into the money market Friday while Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it's ready to inject liquidity again, underscoring that Asia-Pacific central banks remain determined to fight off the credit crisis engulfing global financial markets. (published 0332 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:AUSTRALIA RBA SUPPORTS AUD, FIRST TIME IN SIX YRS    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed Friday that it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets overnight for the first time in six years, to restore liquidity to Australian dollar trading. (published 0250 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =3RD UPDATE:AUSTRALIA RBA FLAGS OUTLOOK RISKS, BUT BIAS TIGHT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Glenn Stevens, said Friday that recent financial market volatility added uncertainty to the economic outlook, but he remains concerned about domestic inflation pressures as demand surges across the economy. (published 0413 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA GOV: AUSTRALIAN BANKS HAVE DIVERSIFIED FUNDING BASE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said Friday he has no regrets about last week's interest rate hike, but is keeping a careful eye on the current market turmoil in deciding the future track for monetary policy. (published 0046 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:AUSTRALIA'S COSTELLO SAYS NO REASON FOR BANKS TO HIKE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said Friday there's no reason for Australia's major banks to raise their interest rates, despite the increased cost of borrowing stemming from the U.S. subprime mortgage crisis. (published 0359 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA PBOC SELLS CNY101B 3-YR BONDS IN SPECIAL SALE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold CNY101 billion worth of three-year bonds in a special sale Friday to control liquidity, it said in a statement. (published 0358 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF SHINOHARA: CLOSELY WATCHING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  point man said Friday he will closely watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves after the yen surged sharply overnight in New York. (published 0030 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:PHILIPPINE BUDGET IN SURPLUS JUL,BACK ON FISCAL TRACK    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines posted a budget surplus of PHP1.6 billion in July, with revenue agencies overshooting collection targets to put the government back on track to hit its fiscal goals for the year. (published 0451 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA JUNE MANUFACTURING SALES UP 2.6% ON YR, +3.2% ON MO    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's manufacturing sales rose 2.6% in June from a year earlier to MYR43.78 billion, the Statistics Department said Friday. (published 0401 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ========== \par  \par WSJE(8/17) BREAKINGVIEWS: AVOIDING CREDIT TURMOIL    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 THE RATINGS agencies are the whipping boys for the credit crunch. They certainly deserve some of the blame. But what sort of punishment? The reaction of politicians will be to pile on the red tape. Barney Frank, chairman of the U.S. House of Representatives' Financial Services Committee, and Charlie McCreevy, the European Union's internal-market commissioner, are limbering up for a fight. (published 0432 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(8/17) CREDIT MARKETS: NEW VILLAIN IN MARKET DRAMA: CP    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commercial paper, the usually humdrum market for short-term debt held by money-market funds and used by companies to finance their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has suddenly taken center stage in the credit crunch. (published 0313 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =RATE FUTURES REPORT: MARKET SEES FED SLASHING TO 4.25% IN '07    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. interest rate futures prices soared for the third straight day Thursday to levels indicating the market expects the Federal Reserve to cut the benchmark rate a full percentage point to 4.25% this year. (published 2008 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: FED SENSITIVE TO PULSE OF ECONOMY, NOT MARKETS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the growing calls for the Federal Reserve to step in and "save" markets from their current misery, it's important to remember the Fed is concerned with the overall monetary system as it relates to the economy as a whole, not with particular markets or financial institutions. (published 1910 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MORTGAGE WOES CAUSE BANKRUPTCY FILINGS TO CREEP UP    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bankruptcy filings may have fallen nearly 50% to 751,056 in the year ended June 30 from the 1.5 million cases filed in the prior-year period. But don't let those numbers fool you. (published 1902 GMT) [ 17-08-07 0504GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070817e38h0004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
