\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day   \b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:AUSTRALIA RBA SUPPORTS AUD, FIRST TIME IN SIX YRS    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Australia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed Friday that it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets overnight for the first time in six years, to restore liquidity to Australian dollar trading. (published 0250 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par *COSTELLO: AUSTRALIAN REAL ECONOMY GROWING ABOVE 3% (published 0241 GMT)  \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA GOVERNOR SAYS ECONOMIC FUNDAMENTALS STRONG    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said Friday that Australia's economic fundamentals remain in strong shape despite the recent state of markets. (published 0225 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA GOV: AUSTRALIAN BANKS HAVE DIVERSIFIED FUNDING BASE    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said Friday he has no regrets about last week's interest rate hike, but is keeping a careful eye on the current market turmoil in deciding the future track for monetary policy. (published 0046 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA RBA FLAGS OUTLOOK RISKS, BUT BIAS TIGHT    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Glenn Stevens, said Friday that recent financial market volatility has added uncertainty to the outlook for the economy, but he said there is a risk that inflation pressures will be more difficult to handle. (published 0201 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA GOVERNOR: ELECTION WON'T AFFECT RBA DECISION MAKING    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said Friday that the upcoming general election won't affect RBA policy making decisions. (published 0056 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF JAPAN INJECTS Y1.2 TRILLION INTO MONEY MARKET    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Friday injected Y1.2 trillion into the short-term money market at its regular 0020 GMT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0038 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF SHINOHARA: CLOSELY WATCHING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOVES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  point man said Friday he will closely watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves after the yen surged sharply overnight in New York. (published 0030 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE GOVT RECORDS PHP1.6B BUDGET SURPLUS IN JULY    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines posted a budget surplus of PHP1.6 billion in July, with revenue agencies overshooting collection targets to put the government back on track to hit its fiscal goals for the year. (published 0251 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ========== \par  \par =RATE FUTURES REPORT: MARKET SEES FED SLASHING TO 4.25% IN '07    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. interest rate futures prices soared for the third straight day Thursday to levels indicating the market expects the Federal Reserve to cut the benchmark rate a full percentage point to 4.25% this year. (published 2008 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: FED SENSITIVE TO PULSE OF ECONOMY, NOT MARKETS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the growing calls for the Federal Reserve to step in and "save" markets from their current misery, it's important to remember the Fed is concerned with the overall monetary system as it relates to the economy as a whole, not with particular markets or financial institutions. (published 1910 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MORTGAGE WOES CAUSE BANKRUPTCY FILINGS TO CREEP UP    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bankruptcy filings may have fallen nearly 50% to 751,056 in the year ended June 30 from the 1.5 million cases filed in the prior-year period. But don't let those numbers fool you. (published 1902 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =THE SKEPTIC: LIQUIDITY CRUNCH HAS ONLY JUST BEGUN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current liquidity crunch is not over and financial markets may be on the brink of a crisis that could surpass the emerging markets crisis of 1998. (published 1501 GMT) [ 17-08-07 0300GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070817e38h0002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
