\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  cenbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  on A$ overnight   \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2007\par 02:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst quote, liquidity injection)   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Aug 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets overnight in an effort to restore some liquidity to the market for the Australian dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) dealt in thin and disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to restore some liquidity," a Reserve Bank spokeswoman said. She had no other information.   \par \par \uc2 The RBA has been routinely selling Australian dollars in the last few years as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose. The last time it bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a net basis in a month was back in late 2001.   \par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar <AUD=> had slid to a fresh five-month low of $0.7818 against the U.S. dollar in New York as risk aversion gripped global markets amid fears of a funding crisis.   \par \par \uc2 "It definitely helped in adding liquidity to the Aussie dollar at a time when it was gapping significantly," said Jo Masters, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 Macquarie Bank.\par \par \uc2 "The Aussie is now almost 100 points (or one cent) higher than its overnight lows which shows their action helped restore some liquidity. Having said that, the Aussie is caught up in this entire tide of de-leveraging that is happening in global markets."   \par \par \uc2 The Aussie <AUD=> extended losses to fall to as as low as $0.7781 in early local trade on Friday, its weakest since March 9, according to Reuters data, but by 11:00 am (0100 GMT) it had recovered to $0.7915/20 against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 In a testimony to a parliamentary committee, RBA Governor Glenn Stevens said recent developments in credit markets added uncertainty to the economic outlook.   \par \par \uc2 Financial markets have been rocked by the U.S. subprime mortgage mess which has sparked a global credit squeeze and seen investors scurrying into safe-haven assets.   \par \par \uc2 That has effectively raised the cost of borrowing and the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday once again pumped in a large amount of funds into the banking system to boost liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 In its regular daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) added A$3.87 billion ($3.07 billion) in cash to the banking system, above a usual daily average of around A$1.8 billion. It pumped in A$3.04 billion on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the U.S. Federal Reserve added $17 billion of reserves to the banking system, which was somewhat larger than typical for such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 AUSTRALIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|AUF|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070817e38h0000x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
