\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar tumbles to 8-\u189\'00\'BD month low on risk worry   \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2007\par 23:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Aug 17 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> tumbled over 4 percent to eight and a half month lows in volatile trade on Friday, hit by another wave of selling on increasing concerns over credit sector problems.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi staged a brief recovery in early trade, after plunging as much as 5 percent on Thursday, but it lost ground as Japanese investors ditched high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on further weakness in the equities market.   \par \par \uc2 "People keep thinking it's ready for a consolidation but the sellers keep coming in," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New Zealand.   \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT the kiwi was at $0.6711/14, after briefly falling to an 8-\u189\'00\'BD month low of $0.6698 <NZD=D4> and down 4.3 percent from a session high of around $0.7010. It fetched $0.6918/20 in late local trade on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Against the yen it tumbled to an 11-month low of 75.16 yen <NZDJPY=R>, down 6 percent from a session high above 80 yen.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi has plunged 17 percent against the U.S. dollar and 23 percent versus the yen after hitting its highest levels in over 20 years in late July, as investors rushed to unwind carry trades, which involve borrowing in low yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest high yielders like the kiwi and Aussie dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the lack of liquidity in the market had added to the recent volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to provide desperately needed liquidity by buying Australian dollars.   \par \par \uc2 RBA Governor Glenn Stevens said the amount bought had been small but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood ready to act from time to time when markets were disorderly.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bonds weakened, with the benchmark 10-year bond <NZG1217=RNZL> yield rising 6 basis points to 6.26 percent following recent strong gains.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|AUF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070819e38g000j3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
