though \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept interest rates unchanged since December last year, financial markets are pricing in a rate hike by October as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to check inflationary pressures in a robustly growing economy.   \par \par \uc2 * The yen <JPY=> was mired near 4-\u189\'00\'BD year lows against the U.S. dollar on a view that Japanese interest rates are unlikely to rise in a hurry.   \par \par \uc2 * Reuters/Jefferies CRB Index <.CRB> down 0.44 percent.   \par \par \uc2 * Industrial metal prices were mixed on the London Metals Exchange as lead prices scaled new peaks while copper prices dipped.   \par \par \uc2 * U.S. crude for delivery in August <CLQ7> settled 49 cents higher or 0.7 percent at $69.14 a barrel, trading from $68.17 to $69.50. Resistance was at $70, with support at $67.55.   \par \par \uc2 * Spot gold <XAU=> was quoted at $653.90/655.40 an ounce in early Asian trade, compared with $653.60/655.10 an ounce in late New York trade on Friday, where it edged up from $651.30/652.80 an ounce a day earlier.   \par \par \uc2 * Aussie bond futures rose, drawing comfort from a sell-off in global equities and tailing U.S. Treasuries.   \par \par \uc2 * U.S. Treasury debt prices rose on Friday, halting a two-day decline, as nervous investors dumped stocks and shifted into government bonds as fresh fears on the subprime mortgage market reverberated across financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 * Three-year Aussie bond futures rose 0.02 points to 93.575 while the 10-year bond contract dropped 0.015 points to 93.75.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-DOLLAR/BONDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070627e36o001y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
